# Source: https://github.com/arq5x/bedtools2/issues/1069
#   https://genome.ucsc.edu/goldenPath/help/bigBed.html
# Symptom: chromosomes are not in a consistent sort order; a record for
#   "chr2" appears after records for "chr20", then "chr3" etc.  Tools that
#   require -sorted input (bedtools intersect -sorted, bedToBigBed) error out:
#   "Sorted input specified, but the file has the following out of order record".
#   Arises when genomic coordinates are sorted lexicographically ("chr10" < "chr2")
#   rather than by natural chromosome order.
chr1	100	200	feature001	0	+
chr10	500	600	feature002	0	+
chr2	1000	1100	feature003	0	+
chr20	5000	5100	feature004	0	+
chr3	8000	8100	feature005	0	+
